{"sourceSha256": "c8755d23cf08eaba1dec7dd403d6f3eb30c7a57ba34b9f7cb887d91c9e5db92a", "text": "Dear Dr Dutz,\n\nRe: Mrs. Sandra Peterson\nDOB: 01/01/1929\n\n| am writing to refer this patient, a 91-year-old widow who has been hospitalised due to\ndehydration secondary to an upper respiratory tract infection and polypharmacy and is due\nto discharge today.\n\nMrs Peterson was initially admitted via ambulance on 20/03/2020, with a history of 3 falls\nover the past week. Augmentin was used to control the infection and saline was\nadministered intravenously to alleviate dehydration. Her blood pressure was severely high\n(190/90) even though she had been taking 6 antihypertensive drugs. As a result, her\nmedications were reviewed and some of the drugs were adjusted or discontinued.\n\nOverall, her condition has significantly improved and she will be discharged today. Her vital\nsigns are normal, although she is has mild confusion and intermittent coughing. Her current\nantihypertensive medications aré metoprolol 25mg twice daily and candesartan 16mg in the\nmorning. She has been advised to continue Augmentin 500mg 12 hourly for 5 days. Her\n\nmedications require close monitoring and her daughter requires education regarding her\nShe ts currently living with her daughter anc has a medical history of Alzheimer’s dementia,\nosteoporosis, hypertension anc hypercholesterolemia. She has no regular GP.\n\n| would appreciate it if you could take over her care for ongoing management.\n\nYours sincerely,\nfing Plysici", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr Dutz,\n\nRe: Mrs. Sandra Peterson\nDOB: 01/01/1929\n\n| am writing to refer this patient, a 91-year-old widow who has been hospitalised due to\ndehydration secondary to an upper respiratory tract infection and polypharmacy and is due\nto discharge today.\n\nMrs Peterson was initially admitted via ambulance on 20/03/2020, with a history of 3 falls\nover the past week. Augmentin was used to control the infection and saline was\nadministered intravenously to alleviate dehydration. Her blood pressure was severely high\n(190/90) even though she had been taking 6 antihypertensive drugs. As a result, her\nmedications were reviewed and some of the drugs were adjusted or discontinued.\n\nOverall, her condition has significantly improved and she will be discharged today. Her vital\nsigns are normal, although she is has mild confusion and intermittent coughing. Her current\nantihypertensive medications aré metoprolol 25mg twice daily and candesartan 16mg in the\nmorning. She has been advised to continue Augmentin 500mg 12 hourly for 5 days. Her\n\nmedications require close monitoring and her daughter requires education regarding her\nShe ts currently living with her daughter anc has a medical history of Alzheimer’s dementia,\nosteoporosis, hypertension anc hypercholesterolemia. She has no regular GP.\n\n| would appreciate it if you could take over her care for ongoing management.\n\nYours sincerely,\nfing Plysici", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2263.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr Dutz,", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr Dutz,", "x": 0.00884, "y": 0.00643, "width": 0.14141, "height": 0.02071, "confidence": 0.936, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.00884, "width": 0.14141, "confidence": 0.964}, {"text": "Dr", "x": 0.06673, "width": 0.02165, "confidence": 0.933}, {"text": "Dutz,", "x": 0.09854, "width": 0.0517, "confidence": 0.911}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Re: Mrs. Sandra Peterson\nDOB: 01/01/1929", "lines": [{"text": "Re: Mrs. Sandra Peterson", "x": 0.00928, "y": 0.0625, "width": 0.26204, "height": 0.01393, "confidence": 0.95, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.00928, "width": 0.03182, "confidence": 0.956}, {"text": "Mrs.", "x": 0.04817, "width": 0.04419, "confidence": 0.937}, {"text": "Sandra", "x": 0.09987, "width": 0.07247, "confidence": 0.958}, {"text": "Peterson", "x": 0.17941, "width": 0.09191, "confidence": 0.948}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text